    {
      "id": 234973,
      "name": "MindWanderer",
      "username": "MindWanderer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
      "created_at": "2021-02-03T19:12:19.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Ocean (seeing a theme here) and Wind-Lightning.&nbsp; Wind-Lightning can grant +1 Range to Ocean almost every round, which means it never has to worry about pushing its presence out of the ocean to hit coastal lands at Range 0.&nbsp; This accelerates it and boosts its effectiveness dramatically.&nbsp; The Fast that comes with it is a nice bonus, too.</p>\n<p>Ocean and Finder&nbsp;<em>should</em>&nbsp;work, but it never seems to pay off like we want.&nbsp; Ocean always has plenty to do without treating inland lands as coasts, and other spirits have plenty to do without pushing inland invaders into the Ocean.&nbsp; I have had some nice finishers where I drown 3 Cities with a single action, though.</p>\n<p>I actually like Lure with Many Minds just as much as Sharp Fangs.&nbsp; Lure also places and loves Beasts, though it's not so single-minded about it.&nbsp; And Many Minds lets it create new kill zones more easily.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:11:11.772Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 69,
      "reads": 26,
      "readers_count": 25,
      "score": 365.2,
